{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "run": 2,
  "simulation_id": "sim-02",
  "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round1_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B007",
        "laureates": [
          "Masato Sagawa",
          "John J. Croat"
        ],
        "citation": "for the discovery of neodymium-iron-boron permanent magnets"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B009",
    "B017"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "B007 remains my preferred configuration. Nd-Fe-B magnets are a sharply identifiable new magnetic-material class whose exceptional performance has been repeatedly established, physically understood, and deployed for decades. Sagawa and Croat provide unusually compact attribution for independently decisive developments. The achievement also joins a fundamental advance in magnetic materials to durable consequences in motors, electronics, and energy technology.",
    "case_against": "The principal reservation is whether the discovery can be framed sufficiently as fundamental physics rather than industrial materials engineering. The precise chronology, independence of the two developments, and boundary between the original material discovery and later optimization require archival scrutiny.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll stresses that optical lattice clocks combine extraordinary reproducibility with a decisive magic-wavelength concept by Katori and field-defining realization by Ye.",
        "response": "I agree that B009 has a particularly strong record of independent replication and now appears more mature than my opening reservation implied. It is therefore my leading alternative. I still place B007 first because its material discovery and its long-established physical and technological transformation can be stated more narrowly, whereas a clock citation must carefully separate the lattice-clock architecture from the broader optical-metrology enterprise."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
        "point": "Mehlig argues that dynamical mean-field theory is a mature, experimentally validated framework that made strong local electronic correlations quantitatively tractable.",
        "response": "This reinforces the scientific stature of B017, especially its connection to spectra and real correlated materials. Yet I retain a qualification: DMFT is an evolving methodological framework with broad intertwined foundations and implementations, so allocating its central intellectual credit to three people is less clean than for B007."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "olsson-eva",
        "point": "Olsson supports B007 as a foundational materials invention but emphasizes the need to confirm the relative independence and chronology of the industrial developments.",
        "response": "I share that caution fully. It is not a minor administrative matter: the legitimacy of the compact two-person attribution depends on demonstrating that each credited contribution belongs to the original discovery rather than to subsequent manufacturing development."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the original Nd-Fe-B discovery meets the intended threshold as a physics discovery rather than a materials-engineering invention.",
      "The exact priority and indispensable contributions in the parallel Sagawa and Croat developments."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
